<p>The UK entered the first of up to five 10-day confirmation periods yesterday. Should the monetary gap remain above +5 per cent for each of these periods the UK's green rate should devalue on 5 June 1997. On the basis of exchange rates from 16-17 April, the RMG for the UK is greater than +5 per cent at 5.815 per cent. It is therefore currently forecast to enter a second confirmation period on 26 April. All currencies with negative average RMGs for the period will be devalued on 26 April by reducing their gaps to zero. Hence devaluations are currently forecast for the Belgian, Dutch, German and Austrian green rates. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is suspended.</p>
